# The lean PLE build (ET_PLE_ONLY): one model's program and weights in their own
# flash partitions, in the N16R8's real 16 MB layout (QEMU's esp32s3 machine
# models fixed SPI flash chips and rejects a 32 MB image). The zoo blobs are
# compiled out; everything else is the identical runtime.
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions_ple.csv"
# PSRAM stays OFF: the QEMU ssi_psram device is hardwired 32 MB
# regardless of CONFIG_SPIRAM_TYPE (that knob only picks octal), and mapping it
# consumes the whole MMU vaddr window -- partition mmap then fails before the model
# ever loads. In QEMU, internal RAM has to carry the whole plan.
